Attendance calculations

For a simple class-count-based model:

Attendance percentage = (Classes Attended / Total Classes Conducted) × 100.

For example:

Classes conducted: 50

Classes attended: 40

Classes missed: 10

Attendance: 80%.

Clearly document how cancelled classes, excused absences, and approved corrections affect the calculation.

Do not assume that every institution uses the same attendance calculation method. Make the calculation method configurable to reflect the institution’s verified policy.

If no classes have been conducted, display “Not available yet” rather than dividing by zero.

